    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "buffer.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Add last_char on impl TextBuffer. Use let-else. let len = self.len().0; let Some(index) = len.checked_sub(1) else { return None; }; then self.char_at(Offset(index)). Do not match Option by hand. Do not nest an if inside an if. Do not touch char_at, len, line_count, line_col, offset, slice, or apply. The existing test char_at_is_none_past_the_end stays green. The test last_char_is_none_when_empty checks TextBuffer::from_str of an empty string returns None. The buffer ab returns Some('b'). The buffer \u00e9 returns Some('\u00e9'). Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines."
  },
